/// The benchmark from Crafting Interpreters: naive recursive Fibonacci, timed.
///
/// It measures function-call overhead more than arithmetic -- fib(30) makes
/// about 2.7 million calls -- which is exactly what a tree-walker pays most for
/// and what compiling is meant to fix.
///
/// N is 30 deliberately: the call count is exponential, so fib(40) is already
/// ~100x this and fib(60) is about a million times longer than you want to wait.
///
/// Not a ctest program: it prints a duration, so there is nothing stable to
/// compare against the interpreter.
///
function Fib(N) : Integer;
begin
    if N < 2 then Exit N;

    Exit Fib(N - 2) + Fib(N - 1);
end

begin
    var Start := clock();

    WriteLn(Fib(30));
    WriteLn(clock() - Start);
end
